---
interface Props {
  storyHref: string;
  excluded?: boolean;
  introductionHref: string;
}
const { storyHref, introductionHref, excluded = false } = Astro.props;
const composer = (path: string) => {
  const url = new URL(path, "https://composer.loftwah.com");
  url.searchParams.set("from", "woodhouse-edition");
  if (excluded) url.searchParams.set("analytics", "off");
  return url.href;
};
---

<section id="build" class="edition-builder" aria-labelledby="builder-title">
  <header>
    <h2 id="builder-title">Make the parts work together.</h2>
    <p>
      App Composer is a studio for building web apps with a coding agent. Start with a creator page,
      a photo guestbook or an app with editable content. Keep the source in your project; use the
      app’s own administration for everyday changes.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="edition-builder__spread">
    <figure>
      <a href={composer("/s/fictional-harbour-notes")} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <img
          src="/share/app-composer/harbour-notes-owner-result-v1-20261023.png"
          alt="The fictional Harbour Notes guestbook shows that new postcards are closed while its approved lantern-and-tide note remains published."
          width="1200"
          height="1007"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <span>Open the hosted Harbour Notes example ↗</span>
      </a>
      <figcaption>
        Hosted owner example v1 · reviewed 23 October 2026. Fictional content, approved in the app’s
        own administration; new submissions are now paused.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div>
      <h3>Approve the note. Then close the book to new arrivals.</h3>
      <p>
        The request was simple: “Make a fictional harbour visitor book. Let me review notes before
        they appear.” The owner set up a separate guestbook in Composer, received a pending note and
        approved it in the protected owner tools. The approved note appeared in the owning app.
      </p>
      <p>
        Then came a small change: “Pause new postcards, keep the approved note.” The app now says
        submissions are closed, and the published note is still there. Existing content and the
        owner’s permissions stayed in place.
      </p>
      <p class="edition-boundary">
        This is an existing owner’s fictional demonstration using supported configuration and
        controls. It does not establish automatic app generation, new-customer onboarding or a
        public approval-count report. Receiving, approving and featuring a postcard are separate
        operations; this example did not feature it.
      </p>
      <div class="edition-actions">
        <a
          class="home-action"
          href={composer("/s/fictional-harbour-notes")}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Inspect the published result ↗
        </a>
        <a href={composer("/manage#analytics-proof")} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          See how owner tools connect ↗
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="edition-builder__spread">
    <figure>
      <a href={composer("/demo")} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
        <img
          src="/share/app-composer/composition-workbench-20261023.png"
          alt="Composer’s public workbench shows a guestbook source and a creator page side by side, with local demonstration controls."
          width="1440"
          height="1000"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <span>Open the working composition ↗</span>
      </a>
      <figcaption>
        Public Composer demonstration, captured 23 October 2026. Fictional content and changes on
        this device; these controls do not publish a real postcard.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
    <div>
      <h3>A photo can appear in two places. Publication still belongs to its source.</h3>
      <p>
        In the workbench, publish the fictional postcard in the guestbook and feature it on the
        creator page. Hide it at the source and see the controlled feature follow. A creator can
        curate a page without taking over the guestbook’s content or editing tools.
      </p>
      <div class="edition-actions">
        <a class="home-action" href={composer("/demo")} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Try the composition ↗
        </a>
        <a href={introductionHref}>Read the practical introduction ↗</a>
      </div>
      <p class="edition-boundary">
        Independent apps also mean separate contracts and versions to maintain. Hiding a source
        controls future reads, not copies someone already downloaded.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <dl class="edition-builder__routes">
    <div>
      <dt>See what the hosted example records.</dt>
      <dd>
        <p>
          The saved report contains fictional demo Open actions. An opening is not a successful
          contribution, a published postcard or customer adoption. It is separate from the
          workbench’s local state and from completed Link Checks.
        </p>
        <a
          href={composer("/reports/r971f5140bbe0c84c8147a64b")}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          Inspect the permitted report ↗
        </a>
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Understand the owner’s next action.</dt>
      <dd>
        <p>
          The management guide shows how supported app administration and reporting connect.
          Existing owners use their protected instance admin; a public example does not grant those
          permissions.
        </p>
        <a href={composer("/manage#analytics-proof")} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Explore management & reporting ↗
        </a>
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Shape a version of your own.</dt>
      <dd>
        <p>
          Init prepares the configuration and build request for your coding agent. You choose the
          content and services. Exporting the request does not provision or publish an app.
        </p>
        <a href={composer("/init?start=composition")} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          Configure a composition ↗
        </a>
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
  <p class="edition-builder__continuation">
    Prefer a small standalone tool?{" "}
    <a href={composer("/launch-kit")} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Explore Night Signal and its launch assets ↗
    </a>
    <br />
    <a href={storyHref}>Inspect the separate completed Link Check story ↗</a>
  </p>
</section>
